      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-light leading-tight tracking-tight mb-6">How much does a tradie website cost in Australia?</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 font-light leading-relaxed mb-4">Whether you're a plumber, sparky, chippy or builder, a good website is one of the cheapest ways to win more jobs. Here's what a tradie website actually costs in 2026 — and what it needs to turn Google searches into phone calls.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-10">By Aman Singh · Build First Site</p>

      <div class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light space-y-5">
        <h2 class="text-2xl mt-10 text-gray-900 font-medium">The short answer</h2>
        <p>A professional tradie website in Australia typically costs <strong>AU$1,500–4,000</strong>. A simple, high-converting one-pager with tap-to-call and a quote form starts around AU$1,200; a fuller site with service-area pages and local SEO runs AU$2,500–4,000. Compared to what one extra job a month is worth, it pays for itself fast.</p>

        <div class="border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden my-8">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-gray-500 text-left"><tr><th class="p-4 font-medium">Site type</th><th class="p-4 font-medium">Typical AU cost</th><th class="p-4 font-medium">Best for</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
              <tr><td class="p-4">One-page site</td><td class="p-4 font-medium">AU$1,200–2,000</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-500">Solo tradies wanting calls fast</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-4">Multi-page + local SEO</td><td class="p-4 font-medium">AU$2,500–4,000</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-500">Established trades, multiple services/suburbs</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-4">Site + booking/quotes system</td><td class="p-4 font-medium">AU$4,000–7,000</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-500">Teams wanting online quote/booking flow</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl mt-10 text-gray-900 font-medium">Do tradies actually need a website?</h2>
        <p>Yes — and here's why. When someone's hot water system fails, they Google "emergency plumber near me" and call one of the first businesses that looks legit. If all you have is a Facebook page, you're invisible for that search. A fast website with reviews, your service area, and a tap-to-call button wins that job. Paired with a free <strong>Google Business Profile</strong>, it also puts you on Google Maps for local searches — where most trade work actually comes from.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl mt-10 text-gray-900 font-medium">What a tradie website must include</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Tap-to-call phone number</strong> — front and centre, on every screen. Most trade enquiries are phone calls.</li>
          <li><strong>Quote request form</strong> — for the ones who won't call, capture the job before they move on.</li>
          <li><strong>Service area &amp; suburbs</strong> — so you rank for "[trade] in [suburb]" and customers know you cover them.</li>
          <li><strong>Real photos of your work</strong> — before/afters build instant trust.</li>
          <li><strong>Reviews</strong> — a few genuine ones outperform any sales copy.</li>
          <li><strong>Licence &amp; insurance</strong> — shows you're legit and compliant.</li>
          <li><strong>Fast load + mobile-first</strong> — customers are on their phone, often in a hurry.</li>
          <li><strong>Local SEO &amp; schema</strong> — so Google understands where you work and what you do.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We recently built exactly this kind of site for a Sydney emergency plumber — conversion-first, local SEO baked in, Lighthouse 95+. You can see the approach on our <a href="/#work" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">portfolio</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl mt-10 text-gray-900 font-medium">What drives the price up or down</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Number of services/suburbs</strong> — more service-area pages means more local reach, but more to build.</li>
          <li><strong>Booking or online quotes</strong> — handy for teams, adds cost.</li>
          <li><strong>Content ready or not</strong> — supplying your own photos and details saves money.</li>
          <li><strong>DIY vs custom</strong> — a AU$399 template rarely ranks or converts; a purpose-built tradie site does.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl mt-10 text-gray-900 font-medium">Common questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 mt-4">
          <div><p class="text-gray-900 font-medium">How much does a plumber or electrician website cost?</p><p>The same AU$1,500–4,000 range applies to most trades. Emergency trades benefit most from a fast, call-focused one-pager plus local SEO.</p></div>
          <div><p class="text-gray-900 font-medium">Will a website get me more jobs?</p><p>Combined with a Google Business Profile and a few reviews, yes — it captures the "near me" searches that currently go to competitors.</p></div>
          <div><p class="text-gray-900 font-medium">Do I need to pay monthly?</p><p>No. We build one-off sites you own outright, with tiny hosting costs — no locked monthly plan. See our <a href="/how-much-does-a-website-cost-australia/" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">full cost guide</a>.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

